      "content": "The words themselves feel like they're falling apart, just like everything else. It's like there's no language left for what I'm feeling. I just sit here, and the only thing that feels real is the cold metal of my blade against my palm. It's the only thing that hasn't lied to me or abandoned me. It's just waiting there in the dark. What do you see when you look at me? Do you see a story that needs a new chapter, or just... an ending that finally makes sense?",
      "source": "evaluator"
